    "rev-title": {
      "type": "Text",
      "left": 40, "top": 700,
      "text": "REVISING MY OWN ARGUMENT — the rain objection is weaker than I claimed",
      "fontColor": "#c8d8f0", "fontSize": 13
    },
    "rev-body": {
      "type": "Text",
      "left": 40, "top": 726,
      "text": "I said a strip kills the density signal. Drawing it, that is only half right.\n\nA strip loses FALL DISTANCE — ~3 cells instead of ~38, so an individual stream barely moves before it dies.\nBut density is encoded as HOW MANY COLUMNS ARE LIT, not how far each falls, and a wide strip has MORE\ncolumns to light: ~45 at 1000px versus ~9 in a 200px rail. Idle-2 vs effort-40 still reads as sparse vs\ndense — arguably more legibly, because you see the whole field at once instead of scanning a column.\n\nWhat is genuinely lost is the MOTION quality: rain that falls three cells reads as flicker, not as rain.\nThat is an aesthetic loss, not a signal loss, and it is a fair trade for not spending a window column.",
      "fontColor": "#c8d0e0", "fontSize": 11
    },
    "cost-title": {
      "type": "Text",
      "left": 40, "top": 862,
      "text": "WHAT B ACTUALLY COSTS",
      "fontColor": "#c8d8f0", "fontSize": 13
    },
    "cost-body": {
      "type": "Text",
      "left": 40, "top": 888,
      "text": "· The detail view loses ~110px of height permanently — on every ticket, decision, file and graph view.\n· The face is small and pinned left; at 220px it is cramped against the bubble with ~126px of text width.\n· Not a slot, so no isVisible / sizeOf / persistence / `clide panel resize` — Epic C must hand-roll a\n  collapse toggle and its own persisted height to keep D-6 parity, or go without.\n· One insertion point though: _ContextSlot at slot_host.dart:349-362 becomes a Column. Much less\n  surface area than a new slot — no slot_id, no layout_preset, no drag_resize sign-flip trap.",
      "fontColor": "#c8d0e0", "fontSize": 11
    }
